ing the physical plant, performs other duties as assigned MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Graduate of standard high school or equivalent, 10 years of combined training and experience in the maintenance and operation of physical plant systems, including the associated plumbing hearing ventilation air conditioning and electrical systems. SALARY: Commensurate with background and experience. INSTITUTION: Cameron University ( www.cameron.edu ) is a state-supported regional institution located in Lawton, Oklahoma, that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. Dedicated to excellence, the university provides a wide range of economic, cultural, and educational opportunities for the betterment of all citizens. Master’s-level graduate degrees are offered in business, behavioral sciences and education; baccalaureate programs are offered in more than forty disciplines, and associate degrees are offered in many other studies. The close proximity of Fort Sill contributes to an area rich in cultural diversity and provides the opportunity for many cooperative efforts. The combined community of Lawton/Fort Sill has a population of more than 100,000 and is located adjacent to the picturesque Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge. HOW TO APPLY: All applicants, to include those presently employed by the University, should contact the Human Resources Office, located in the Administration Building to complete an application, or download download the application and return to the Human Resources office. Applicants may also email their information to hr@cameron.edu . DEADLINE: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled; however, only candidates whose applications are received by October 15, 2026 are assured of receiving full consideration. EEO/AA Employer/Vets/Disability JOB #: A1359A This position is located at 2800 W. Gore Blvd, \nLawton, OK. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply E-Verify Disclosure (English) Disclosure (Spanish) Affirmative Action Plan Recruitment Information