      "title": "Assistant Professor or Instructor of Organizational Leadership & Business",
      "description": "Assistant Professor or Instructor of Organizational Leadership & Business - 2800 W. Gore Blvd, Lawton, Oklahoma, United States - Cameron University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... Cameron University Career Opportunities chevron_left Cameron University Jobs Apply Assistant Professor or Instructor of Organizational Leadership & Business ﻿ Administration/Professional Lawton, OK • ID: F1281F • Full-Time/Regular Job Description: Assistant Professor or Instructor of Organizational Leadership & Business The School of Business seeks to hire a full-time Assistant Professor (preferred) or Instructor in Organizational Leadership and Business to begin teaching in Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. Responsibilities include teaching a wide array of organizational leadership and business courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels based on faculty expertise/training and program needs. Faculty are expected to teach in multiple formats, including distance learning, online, and face-to-face; perform department and university service; support student scholarship; and conduct research in their field. Other responsibilities include student advisement, assisting with program and department assessment and development, and supporting student organizations and events. Other duties as required. SUPERVISION: The position will report to the chair of the McMahon School of Business. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: A PhD in Organizational Leadership or a related business field is needed to qualify for the Assistant Professor rank, and would enable the faculty member to teach in the MSOL program. A Master’s degree in Organizational Leadership or a related business field is needed to qualify at the Instructor rank. Applicants who are doctoral degree candidates may be considered for the Assistant Professor position, but if hired and the degree has not been earned by the start of the employment period, the initial appointment will be made at the rank (and salary) of Instructor and will only be converted upon documented completion of the degree, in accordance with the conditions specified in the offer letter. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Expertise in online teaching and Quality Matters would be preferred. SALARY RANGE: Commensurate with education and experience. BENEFITS: Cameron University offers a wide variety of comprehensive programs to benefit our employees. We are proud to offer benefits such as paid medical coverage, ample time off, and employee tuition waiver programs. To view all benefits available to employees, visit: https://www.cameron.edu/hr/faculty-benefits-summary INSTITUTION: Cameron University (www.cameron.edu) is a state-supported regional institution in Lawton, Oklahoma, offering undergraduate and graduate degrees. Dedicated to excellence, the university provides a wide range of economic, cultural, and educational opportunities for the betterment of all citizens. Master ’s-level graduate degrees are offered in business, behavioral sciences, and education; baccalaureate programs are offered in more than forty disciplines, and associate degrees are offered in many other studies. The close proximity of Fort Sill contributes to an area rich in cultural diversity and provides the opportunity for many cooperative efforts. The combined community of Lawton/Fort Sill has a population of more than 100,000 and is located adjacent to the picturesque Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge. A copy of the University’s Annual Security Report, listing crime statistics and university policies, is available by contacting the Office of Public Safety or by accessing the report online at www.cameron.edu/ops. APPLYING: Application materials must be submitted online ( Cameron University Careers ) and must include (1) a cover letter that addresses the applicant’s qualifications for the position, (2) a C.V. or resume that includes a minimum of three professional references with their current contact information, (3) copies of transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable at this time), and (4) a statement of teaching philosophy.  Transcripts must be combined into a single PDF before uploading.  Finalists must satisfactorily complete a background check and have all official transcripts sent directly to the university before the contract period begins. The position will begin in Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. Questions about the position should be directed to Jennifer Ellis, Chair of the McMahon School of Business, at jellis@cameron.edu DEADLINE: Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. EEO/AA Employer/Veteran/Disability This position is located at 2800 W. Gore Blvd, \r\nLawton, OK. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply E-Verify Disclosure (English) Disclosure (Spanish) Affirmative Action Plan Recruitment Information Our Campus CU Campus Map close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/Cameron/Careers/jobs/1795": {
      "title": "Student and Community Engagement Specialist, Duncan Campus",
      "description": "Student and Community Engagement Specialist, Duncan Campus - 3100 W. Bois D'arc, Duncan, Oklahoma, United States - Cameron University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... Cameron University Career Opportunities chevron_left Cameron University Jobs Apply Student and Community Engagement Specialist, Duncan Campus ﻿ Administration/Professional Duncan, OK • ID: A1203E • Full-Time/Regular Student and Community Engagement Specialist JOB DESCRIPTION: The Student and Community Engagement Specialist is based in Duncan, Oklahoma and is responsible for engagement with the Duncan area community and prospective students within the university’s primary service area. The position is also responsible for student engagement activities for the current campus population. This is an entry-level position that reports to the Director of the Duncan Campus. Student Engagement Responsibilities: Develop and implement student engagement opportunities that enhance campus life and support student connection and retention. Collaborate with campus faculty, staff, and student groups to develop programming that supports student success, belonging, and co-curricular learning. Assist with the promotion of student activities through text, email, digital signage, and social media to encourage participation and awareness. Maintain a flexible and creative approach to programming, adapting activities to fit the scale and resources of a small campus environment. Community Engagement Responsibilities: Represent Cameron University through proactive community engagement, including high school visits, presentations, and on- and off-campus events to build awareness and interest in CU Duncan. Guide prospective students and their families through the full enrollment process, including admissions applications, Oklahoma’s Promise, FAFSA, and other pre-college requirements. Build and maintain relationships with area high schools, technical centers, businesses, and community partners to support college readiness and strengthen recruitment pipelines. Provide personalized support to prospective students by assessing needs, identifying educational goals, and assisting with program selection, financial planning, and pathways to degree completion. Conduct outreach (calls, email, social media) on behalf of CU Duncan, and maintain accurate records in the student information system. Communicate consistently with prospective students through multiple channels, addressing inquiries, providing guidance, and connecting them with campus resources to support enrollment and matriculation. Evaluate and process admissions records while ensuring accurate data entry and maintenance within institutional systems. Other Duties: Serves as backup in the Duncan Testing Center and Administrative Office Assists the Duncan campus Director with various special projects Performs and assists with other related duties as assigned Required Knowledge Skills/Abilities Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including public speaking and presentations. Strong organizational, time-management, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Ability to build rapport quickly and work effectively and respectfully with diverse populations, including prospective students and community partners. Proficiency with standard office and digital tools (e.g., Microsoft Office, Adobe Suite) and comfort working in electronic environments, including CRM systems, virtual communication, and social media. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision, including occasional travel for recruitment activities. Ability to perform physical tasks associated with events and outreach, including lifting 10–20 lbs and standing or walking for extended periods. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS An earned bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited university Minimum of two years responsible employment Valid Driver's License PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS 4. Experience in recruitment or student engagement 5. Experience in event planning and promotion 6. Experience working with Slate, Navigate, and/or Banner Salary: 29,500 INSTITUTION: Cameron University (www.cameron.edu) is a state-supported regional institution located in Lawton, Oklahoma, that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. Dedicated to excellence, the university provides a wide range of economic, cultural, and educational opportunities for the betterment of all citizens. Master's-level graduate degrees are offered in business, behavioral sciences, and education; baccalaureate programs are offered in more than forty disciplines, and associate degrees are offered in many other studies. The close proximity of Fort Sill contributes to an area rich in cultural diversity and provides the opportunity for frequent cooperative efforts. The combined community of Lawton/Fort Sill has a population of more than 100,000 and is located adjacent to the picturesque Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge. A copy of the University’s Annual Security Report, listing crime statistics and university policies, is available by contacting the Office of Public Safety or by accessing the report online at www.cameron.edu/ops . APPLYING: Attachments should include a cover letter indicating experience applicable to position, resume , transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this point), as well as the names, emails, and telephone numbers of three professional references. DEADLINE: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. EEO/AA Employer/Vets/Disability This position is located at 3100 W. Bois D'arc, \r\nDuncan, OK. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply E-Verify Disclosure (English) Disclosure (Spanish) Affirmative Action Plan Recruitment Information Our Campus CU Campus Map close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/Cameron/Careers/jobs/1811": {
      "title": "Housing Assistant (HA)",
      "description": "Housing Assistant (HA) - 2800 W. Gore Blvd, Lawton, Oklahoma, United States - Cameron University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... Cameron University Career Opportunities chevron_left Cameron University Jobs Apply Housing Assistant (HA) ﻿ Classified Lawton, OK • ID: 1811-345 • Part-Time Position Description The Housing Assistant (HA) position is a student employment role within the Office of Student Housing and Residence Life at Cameron University for the 2026-2027 academic year. This position is contingent upon available funding and includes a variety of responsibilities related to assisting students, supporting housing operations, and performing general duties necessary for the smooth functioning of university housing. Key Responsibilities: • Office Hours: Maintain set office hours during the day as assigned to ensure availability for students, staff, and visitors, providing a consistent point of contact for questions, concerns, or assistance. • Customer Service: Provide friendly and professional face-to-face assistance to students, staff, and visitors, including helping residents navigate housing services, addressing concerns, and providing guidance on housing policies and procedures. • Communication: Answer phones, handle inquiries, and direct calls as necessary, ensuring timely and accurate information is provided. Communicate effectively with residents regarding work orders, updates, or other housing-related issues. • Administrative Tasks: Assist with filing, paperwork, and other clerical duties, including maintaining records of resident interactions, work orders, and other documentation to support smooth office operations. • Mail and Packages: Sort, distribute, and manage resident mail and packages efficiently, notifying residents of deliveries and helping ensure timely access to their items. • Resident Support: Assist residents with lockouts, submitting and tracking work orders, resolving room or other issues, and providing guidance on housing-related concerns to promote a safe and supportive living environment. • Miscellaneous Duties: Perform additional duties as assigned by Student Housing Professional Staff, which may include giving tours to prospective students and visitors, helping create marketing materials or promotions for housing programs, assisting with photography or content for marketing purposes, and supporting housing events and initiatives. Position Requirements The HA position is open to students who meet the following criteria: • Enrollment: Must be enrolled as a student at Cameron University. • GPA Requirement: Must maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher to apply for and retain the position. Compensation Housing Assistants (HAs) will be compensated at a rate of designated by the supervisor. Working hours may vary depending on the needs of the department. HAs are expected to maintain flexibility in their schedules to accommodate operational requirements, special projects, and emergency situations as needed. EEO/AA/Veterans This position is located at 2800 W. Gore Blvd, \r\nLawton, OK. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply E-Verify Disclosure (English) Disclosure (Spanish) Affirmative Action Plan Recruitment Information Our Campus CU Campus Map close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/Cameron/Careers/jobs/1810": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications and Operations",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications and Operations - 2800 W. Gore Blvd, Lawton, Oklahoma, United States - Cameron University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... Cameron University Career Opportunities chevron_left Cameron University Jobs Apply Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications and Operations ﻿ Hourly Lawton, OK • ID: H1700A-25 • Full-Time/Regular Graduate Assistant – Athletic Communications and Operations Cameron University Athletics, and NCAA DII member of the Lone Star Conference, is seeking candidates for a graduate assistant position in the office of Athletic Communications and Operations. The graduate assistant will assist the Director of Athletic Communications with the successful implementation of various department functions. Responsibilities may include any of the following assignments based on skill-set and experience: · Creative video and digital content, website and other electronic media, and media relations for Cameron’s 13 intercollegiate sports. · Create and post content to athletic department/select athletic programs’ social media accounts. · Assist with FloSports broadcasts and all athletic web stream productions. · Write press releases and game recaps, roster and schedule maintenance on the athletics website, game programs, updating student-athlete and coach bios, media relations, and production of statistics at home events. · Assist with creating other content including photography, capturing video, written features, development and enhancement of records and archives, and general athletic department website maintenance. · Assist with the supervision of athletic events and facilities · Assist or lead with supervision game operation functions such as ticket sales, concession management, crowd management, game worker support, game technology management. · Serves as game administrator for select home contests · Assist with scheduling practices and events in all athletic facilities · Assisting the Director of Athletic Communications with development and implementation of athletic department media campaigns. · Assist with production of presentations for special events · Work both as a member of a team as well as individually with supervision · Other duties as assigned Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required Ability to be admitted into a Cameron University graduate program Ability to work all home athletic games and events- nights and weekends required Ability to work a flexible schedule between 25-29 hours per week in various environments Ability to climb stairs and lift up to 40 lbs may be required Experience with Adobe Creative Suite, including Photoshop and InDesign, is preferred Experience with photography and/or video editing is preferred Experience with website management is preferred · Expertise managing various social media platforms, including but not limited to Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube, and Snapchat is preferred Experience with NCAA statistical programs is preferred Package/Compensation : · Up to nine hours per semester of tuition and mandatory fees, on-campus apartment-style housing waiver, and monthly stipend. Start Date: · This position will begin in January 2027 To Apply: · Interested applicants should must apply online at https://cameronhr.silkroad.com . This position will remain open until filled. EEO/AA Employer/Vets/Disability This position is located at 2800 W. Gore Blvd, \r\nLawton, OK. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply E-Verify Disclosure (English) Disclosure (Spanish) Affirmative Action Plan Recruitment Information Our Campus CU Campus Map close"
