      "description": "Graduate Assistant Tennis Coach, Athletics - 2800 W. Gore Blvd, Lawton, Oklahoma, United States - Cameron University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... Cameron University Career Opportunities chevron_left Cameron University Jobs Apply Graduate Assistant Tennis Coach, Athletics ﻿ Hourly Lawton, OK • ID: H1700A-T • Part-Time POSTED JOB TITLE: Graduate Assistant Tennis Coach - Athletics JOB DESCRIPTION: Cameron University’s Tennis Program is looking for a Graduate Assistant Coach who wants to join a professionally run NCAA Division II athletic program. Duties include, but are not limited to: Assist head coach and coaching staff in daily operations of program, on-court coaching, court maintenance, recruiting, fundraising, and community involvement. Monitoring the academic progress of the student athletes. Assist with driving for team travel and/or recruiting. All responsibilities will be assigned by the head coach including adherence to all rules and regulations of Cameron University, the Lone Star Conference, and the NCAA. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Candidate must have a Bachelor’s degree and a willingness to learn the entire operations of running a college tennis program. Candidate must have an outgoing personality with the desire to enter the coaching field as a career after obtaining a Master’s Degree. Candidate must have a US Driver’s License. SALARY RANGE: $1,000/semester + tuition (up to nine semester hours for four semesters) and fees (mandatory fees only; special and online fees not included) + housing (Campus apartment) waiver INSTITUTION: Cameron University (www.cameron.edu) is a state-supported regional institution located in Lawton, Oklahoma, that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. Dedicated to excellence, the university provides a wide range of economic, cultural, and educational opportunities for the betterment of all citizens. Master's-level graduate degrees are offered in business, behavioral 